-- title:
--   Kernel degree of the quasi-inverse leg is an even power of r
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $r\neq\bar r$ and $N\neq 0$ with $r\nmid N$. The coefficient data consist of: a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero with irreducible uniformiser $\pi$, residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, with fraction field $K_0$; an $\mathcal O$-algebra $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ that is a characteristic-zero domain, $\pi$-adically complete, with $(\pi)$ maximal, every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, and an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$ with $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$. Further: rationals $a,b$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ containing $\mathbb Z$ together with a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to \mathrm{Zp2}\,r\times \mathrm{Zp2}\,r$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord`; a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ with formal coordinates $\theta_0$ exhibiting a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$; a ring map $\iota:\mathrm{Zp2}\,r\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ and a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$; a moduli package $M$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf, together with a family $\eta$ of maps from rigidified objects to points of $M$ satisfying the three conditions that $\eta$ classifies admissible rigidified data up to isomorphism, commutes with base change, and is locally surjective; an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of $\Phi$'s action and $\varpi$ endomorphisms into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image agrees with $r^{-m}M_2(\mathcal O)$; the reduction bridge $\kappa:O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps; and an isogeny $\beta_0:\Phi\to X_0\otimes_\kappa$ of height $4n_0$. Let $B$ be a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, in which $\pi$ and $r$ are nilpotent, $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, $E$ a fake elliptic curve over $B$ with a rigidification $\rho$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$, and $\theta$ formal coordinates exhibiting a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ for $E$. Finally let $\sigma$ be a pair of power series in two variables over $\bar B=B/(\pi)$ which is an $\mathcal O_D$-linear homomorphism from $X_0$ base-changed along the residue leg of $\psi$ to $X$ base-changed to $\bar B$, and assume $\sigma$ represents the quasi-inverse leg $\rho.\varphi'$ followed by $\rho.g_b$ on infinitesimal points: for every ring $B''$ that is simultaneously an algebra over $\bar B$, $B$ and $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ compatibly, every ideal $J$ with $J^{m+1}=0$, every $s:\mathrm{Fin}\,2\to J$ and every $B''$-point $P_A$ of $\rho.A_b$ over the structure map with $P_A$ followed by $\rho.g_A$ equal to $\theta_0(s)$, the composite of $P_A$ with $\rho.\varphi'$ and $\rho.g_b$ equals $\theta$ evaluated at the truncations of $\sigma$ at $s$. The conclusion is that there exists $h\in\mathbb N$ with `HasKernelOfDegree σ (r ^ (2 * h))`: the quotient of $\bar B[[X_1,X_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the two components of $\sigma$ is a finite projective $\bar B$-module whose rank over every field-valued point of $\bar B$ equals $r^{2h}$.
--
--   This is the degree computation for the leg of a rigidification in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of Shimura curves: the series representing the quasi-inverse isogeny $\rho.\varphi'$ on the formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules has finite locally free kernel algebra of degree an even power of $r$. It feeds the construction of admissible rigidified data transported from a fake elliptic curve with given formal coordinates, in `exists_isRigTransport_isAdmissible_of_isFormalModuleVia`.
